symmetry-requirement-d8d607ad.conceptual_definition:
The formula illustrates a fundamental concept in particle physics, particularly in the context of neutrino masses, known as the Seesaw Mechanism. It posits a relationship between a very high energy scale, often associated with the breaking of a grand unified theory (GUT) symmetry, and the very small masses of neutrinos. The equation suggests that if there are heavy right-handed neutrinos with masses around the GUT scale (
 M 
 \sim 10^{15} \text{ GeV}
 ), then the observed light neutrino masses (
 m_\nu 
 \sim 0.03 \text{ eV}
 ) naturally arise as a consequence of this symmetry breaking.

