left-handed-quark-doublet.limits_and_boundary:
This notation is a fundamental building block of the Standard Model and does not have 'limits' in the sense of asymptotic behavior of variables. It describes the fundamental quantum fields and their intrinsic interactions. The concept is valid across all energy scales where the Standard Model is applicable. If one were to consider a hypothetical scenario where the weak interaction strength (related to the W boson mass, 
$M_W$
) approaches zero, the notion of a distinct weak doublet would become less pronounced, but this is not a physical limit of the doublet structure itself.
